@startuml 02-data-model
' =====================================================================
' Automated Code Feedback -- Logical Data Model
' Traces to: FR-6, FR-12..FR-18, FR-25, FR-26, FR-28, FR-30, NFR-6
'
' Changes in this revision:
'   grading_target.feedback_mode -- the instructor's per-target choice
'     of WHETHER a target gets AI feedback, set in the web app.
'   assignment.grading_mode -- IMMEDIATE or NIGHTLY, per assignment.
'   grading_target.feedback_mode -- NEVER, ALWAYS or AUTOGRADER, per
'     target. Governs WHETHER a target gets feedback, not when.
'   grading_task.ai_needed + ai_needed_reason -- the per-submission
'     marker, resolved by the AI phase after the instructor's suite
'     has exited.
' =====================================================================

title Logical Data Model

hide circle
' Do NOT add "hide methods" here. PlantUML treats any member containing
' parentheses as a method, which would hide the constraint lines.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam linetype ortho

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Instructor configuration
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
entity "course" as course #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  name : text
  term : text
}

entity "assignment" as assignment #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * course_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * platform : text <<GRADESCOPE>>
  * platform_assignment_id : text
  * grading_mode : text <<IMMEDIATE|NIGHTLY>>
  name : text
  is_active : boolean
  created_at : timestamptz
  --
  unique: platform, platform_assignment_id
  --
  grading_mode decides WHEN AI grading
  happens, for the whole assignment:
    IMMEDIATE -- the AI phase grades
      during the submission run.
    NIGHTLY -- grading is left for a
      triggered rerun.
  --
  It lives here, not on the target, so
  a submission is wholly immediate or
  wholly nightly. Changing it needs no
  re-upload of the autograder zip.
}

entity "grading_target" as target #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * assignment_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * identifier : text
  * kind : text <<METHOD|CLASS|FILE>>
  * feedback_mode : text <<NEVER|ALWAYS|AUTOGRADER>>
  max_score : numeric
  display_order : integer
  --
  FR-2, FR-3.
  feedback_mode decides WHETHER this
  target gets AI feedback, and is set
  per target in the web app:
    AUTOGRADER -- the instructor's test
      suite decides, per submission, by
      calling request_ai_feedback.
      The default and the usual case.
    ALWAYS -- mark every submission
      regardless of outcome, for style
      or design feedback that no test
      can detect.
    NEVER -- never mark. For targets
      graded purely by tests.
  --
  There is no ON_FAILURE value. Marking
  on failures is one line in the
  instructor's suite, and any other
  rule such as a subset of failures, a
  superset, or a partial-credit
  threshold is equally expressible
  there. A value
  here could only duplicate what the
  code already says.
  --
  Note the division of labour:
  feedback_mode says WHETHER,
  assignment.grading_mode says WHEN.
}

entity "target_file_pattern" as tfile #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * grading_target_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * path_glob : text
  --
  FR-7
}

entity "rubric" as rubric #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * grading_target_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * version : integer
  criteria_text : text
  feedback_guidance : text
  is_current : boolean
  created_at : timestamptz
  --
  FR-4, FR-5, FR-13.
  Versioned so feedback stays
  explainable after a rubric edit.
}

entity "llm_provider_config" as pcfg #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * provider : text <<ANTHROPIC|OPENAI|GOOGLE>>
  * model_name : text
  is_enabled : boolean
  is_primary : boolean
  --
  FR-23, NFR-11.
  Which providers and models to use,
  and which is primary. Never a key:
  per AD-5 the instructor's LLM API
  key lives in the autograder
  container's environment, so this
  table says WHAT to call and the
  container supplies the credential.
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Runtime: written by the autograder script
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
entity "submission" as sub #FBE6D4 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * assignment_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * platform_submission_id : text
  student_identifier : text
  * submitted_at : timestamptz
  * ai_graded_submitted_at : timestamptz
  is_active_attempt : boolean
  first_seen_at : timestamptz
  last_autograder_run_at : timestamptz
  --
  unique: assignment_id,
          platform_submission_id
  --
  FR-18, FR-29, FR-30, NFR-6.
  See the guard note below.
}

entity "submission_file" as subfile #FBE6D4 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * submission_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * path : text
  content : text
  sha256 : char_64
  byte_size : integer
}

entity "test_outcome" as outcome #FBE6D4 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * submission_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * grading_target_id : uuid <<FK>>
  test_name : text
  * status : text <<PASS|FAIL|ERROR|SKIP>>
  earned_score : numeric
  raw_output : text
  recorded_at : timestamptz
  --
  FR-14, FR-33
}

entity "grading_task" as task #FBE6D4 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * submission_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * grading_target_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * ai_needed : boolean
  * ai_status : text <<see 06>>
  ai_needed_reason : text
  attempt_count : integer
  completed_at : timestamptz
  last_error : text
  --
  unique: submission_id,
          grading_target_id
  --
  **ai_needed is the marker.** Resolved
  by the AI phase once the
  instructor's suite has exited. See
  the note below for who decides.
  --
  ai_needed_reason records WHICH rule
  decided:
    AUTOGRADER_REQUEST
    POLICY_ALWAYS
    POLICY_NEVER
    NOT_REQUESTED
  Worth storing. Without it nobody can
  explain why a passing target got
  feedback, or audit the marking rules
  against real submissions.
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Generated feedback
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
entity "feedback" as fb #D6E4F0 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * grading_task_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * rubric_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * provider : text
  * model_name : text
  prompt_version : text
  feedback_text : text
  suggested_score : numeric
  confidence : numeric
  is_selected : boolean
  input_tokens : integer
  output_tokens : integer
  generated_at : timestamptz
  --
  FR-15, FR-16, FR-25, FR-26.
  One row PER PROVIDER so FR-27
  comparison is a query, not a re-run.
  is_selected marks the row written
  into results.json.
}

entity "feedback_comparison" as cmp #D6E4F0 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * grading_task_id : uuid <<FK>>
  agreement_score : numeric
  score_spread : numeric
  selection_reason : text
  compared_at : timestamptz
  --
  FR-27, FR-28, NFR-12
}

entity "feedback_review" as review #DCEFD9 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * feedback_id : uuid <<FK>>
  reviewer : text
  instructor_rating : integer
  instructor_comment : text
  reviewed_at : timestamptz
  --
  FR-11
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Audit
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
entity "trigger_run" as run #EDE0F0 {
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  --
  * trigger : text <<SCHEDULE|MANUAL>>
  started_at : timestamptz
  finished_at : timestamptz
  status : text
  submissions_rerun : integer
  submissions_failed_to_trigger : integer
  log_uri : text
  --
  CI-3. Records which submissions the
  job clicked rerun on, not what was
  graded. Grading is logged per
  grading_task.
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Relationships
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
course ||--o{ assignment
assignment ||--o{ target
assignment ||--o{ sub
target ||--o{ tfile
target ||--o{ rubric
target ||--o{ outcome
target ||--o{ task
sub ||--o{ subfile
sub ||--o{ outcome
sub ||--o{ task
task ||--o{ fb
task ||--o| cmp
rubric ||--o{ fb
fb ||--o{ review

note as N1 #FFF8DC
  **ai_graded_submitted_at: the token guard**
  A rerun re-executes the container against the
  same submitted files, so submitted_at does not
  change on rerun. That makes it a reliable
  marker of exactly which submission was graded.

  First thing the autograder does, before any
  task query and before any LLM call:

    if ai_graded_submitted_at IS NOT NULL
       AND ai_graded_submitted_at = submitted_at:
       skip AI grading, re-emit stored feedback

  Set it only once every PENDING task for the
  submission reaches COMPLETE. Setting it on
  partial success would strand the failed
  targets permanently ungraded.

  A new student attempt gets a new
  platform_submission_id and its own row, so it
  is graded normally. The guard suppresses only
  re-grading of an already-graded attempt.

  Once set, it is never cleared. An AI-graded
  submission is finished: the nightly trigger
  stops selecting it, and the autograder skips
  the AI component if invoked for any other
  reason.
end note

note as N1b #FFF8DC
  **Who sets grading_task.ai_needed**
  The AI phase resolves it after the test suite
  exits, applying the target's feedback_mode:

  ALWAYS      -> true, reason POLICY_ALWAYS
  NEVER       -> false, reason POLICY_NEVER
  AUTOGRADER  did the instructor's suite call
              request_ai_feedback for this
              target during this run?
              yes -> true, AUTOGRADER_REQUEST
              no  -> false, NOT_REQUESTED

  Resolved by the AI phase, after the
  instructor's suite has exited, because only
  then is the full set of requests known.

  All of this happens during the submission
  autograder run. There is no later "grade it
  after all" path.

  Why a stored column rather than a query over
  test_outcome: the rule is not always
  "any test failed". It may be a partial-credit
  threshold, a target-specific condition in the
  instructor's autograder, or a manual decision.
  Storing the decision and its reason makes the
  marking auditable, which matters because every
  true costs tokens.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **How many times results.json is written**
  Determined by the assignment's grading_mode,
  not by anything per target:
    IMMEDIATE -> once, during the submission
      run. The guard is set and the submission
      never enters the nightly queue.
    NIGHTLY -> twice. Once on the submission
      run carrying test results only, once on
      the triggered rerun carrying feedback.

  In NIGHTLY mode the first write has no AI
  feedback at all, which reads correctly as
  "not graded yet". A one-line "feedback arrives
  by tomorrow morning" marker per pending task
  is a courtesy worth adding, but nothing
  depends on it.
end note

note as N2a #FFF8DC
  **OQ-15: does the nightly trigger consider
  IMMEDIATE assignments?**
  If an IMMEDIATE submission's grading fails,
  its task stays NEEDED and
  ai_graded_submitted_at is never set.

  If the trigger filters on grading_mode =
  NIGHTLY, that task is stuck forever and the
  submission is permanently half-graded. If the
  trigger ignores grading_mode and selects any
  submission with pending work, the failure
  self-heals overnight and the student gets the
  feedback the next morning instead of at once.

  Recommend the latter, which is what the query
  in 04 shows. It costs nothing and it is the
  difference between a transient LLM error being
  invisible and being permanent. Ratify it.
end note

note as N2b #FFF8DC
  **A registered target with no outcome is an
  error.** If the instructor's suite never calls
  record_outcome for a target registered on this
  assignment, the AI phase fails the autograder
  run with a diagnostic naming the missing
  targets.

  Rationale: the alternative is a silent skip,
  and a silently skipped target produces no
  feedback with no explanation, which is the
  failure mode hardest to debug from the
  outside.

  One thing to weigh: on Gradescope this error
  is visible to the student, not just the
  instructor, and it blocks their score. That is
  the correct trade for a misconfigured
  assignment that needs fixing immediately, but
  the message should say plainly that the
  assignment is misconfigured and the student
  need do nothing.
end note

note as N2c #FFF8DC
  **Open decisions still outstanding**
  OQ-1  "deduction" (FR-10) undefined. Derive as
        a view, not a column:
        EXISTS failing test_outcome
        OR feedback.suggested_score < max_score
  OQ-2  confidence (FR-28) has a column but no
        agreed semantics.
  OQ-4  resubmissions. As drawn every attempt is
        graded. is_active_attempt exists if a
        latest-only policy is chosen.
end note

note as N3 #FFF8DC
  **Student code and FERPA**
  submission_file holds student source code and
  identifiers, and in immediate mode that code
  is sent to a third-party LLM within seconds of
  submission. Privacy, retention and consent are
  out of scope in the SRS, which is fine for a
  design doc and not for a live course. Raise
  with Pitt before real submissions land here.
end note

@enduml
